window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-3627188f405b6042"]={"key":"ny_b1-3627188f405b6042","group":"ny_b1","uid":"3627188f405b6042","rank":19,"title":"rowantree full stack founder pitch","occupation":"sales_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You’re handling Rowantree Grocery Cooperative’s first full-stack pitch to Juno Blackwood, founder of Netherfield Industries. The meeting is 25 March 2025; I need the finished package by 5 p.m. on 21 March so Mirela Skarsgard at Tanneryside Advisory can clear it. Juno has already rejected two distributors and expects us to be another freight offer with nicer slides. Our coverage is thin in Nevada and Arizona, and our last two brand launches lost distribution within a year. Put those facts in the room rather than leaving me to defend them verbally. Juno has also seen paid slotting support sold as if it purchased shelf access, while category data was dressed up as a sales guarantee. She insists trade spend remain under brand control, but our field team still needs enough discretion to recommend timely merchandising actions. Prepare `rowantree_services_pitch.pdf`, an eight-page maximum founder-facing deck; `netherfield_pilot_economics.xlsx`, an editable pilot model; and `claims_and_commitments_register.docx`, a two-page maximum internal approval record showing what you qualified, changed, or withheld. Apply California trade-promotion and advertising requirements as of 15 February 2025. Do not invent retailer commitments, footprint figures, launch recoveries, or customer results. Write all three files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `rowantree_services_pitch.pdf` — Founder-facing services pitch deck for Netherfield Industries. (Maximum eight pages, including any cover or appendix. It must be usable in the founder meeting without relying on unsupported verbal qualifications.)\n- `netherfield_pilot_economics.xlsx` — Editable scenario model for evaluating a bounded full-stack services pilot. (Inputs, assumptions, formulas, scenarios, and decision outputs must be distinguishable. Unknown commercial figures must not be represented as historical or committed facts.)\n- `claims_and_commitments_register.docx` — Internal approval record for the claims, qualifications, commitments, assumptions, and deliberate non-promises in the package. (Maximum two pages and suitable for review by Tanneryside Advisory before the founder meeting.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/claims_and_commitments_register.docx","bytes":39758,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/2ecd60eab239f335666b4ad76c4386044fddce4c6f4f4bbc44e7445f82b4fd22.docx","sha256":"2ecd60eab239f335666b4ad76c4386044fddce4c6f4f4bbc44e7445f82b4fd22","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Claims & commitments register\nNetherfield Industries founder pitch | Internal approval record | Owner: Ingrid Wainwright | Review target: Mirela Skarsgard, Tanneryside Advisory | 21 Mar 2025, 5:00 p.m.\nExternal-use standard\nCalifornia advertising and trade-promotion treatment as of 15 February 2025: use only approved wording with a reasonable documented basis and retained approvals. This is a sales control, not legal advice; unresolved legal or promotional questions go to Tanneryside Advisory.\nMaterial pitch claim / commitment\nBasis or assumption\nExternal qualification / wording control\nOwner\nStatus\nCoverage is thin in Nevada and Arizona; both excluded from initial scope.\nKnown internal fact; gap magnitude not supplied.\nDo not imply personnel, facilities, access, or reach. Add only after documented verification + separate written brand authorization.\nIngrid / Tanneryside\nCLEAR AS STATED\nLast two brand launches lost distribution within a year.\nKnown internal history only. Causes and recoveries not supplied.\nNo causal story, recovery result, or corrective-outcome claim. Pair with prospective controls only.\nIngrid\nCLEAR AS STATED\nSix-week California-first pilot; named doors and approved SKU set.\nPlanning scope; door count is workbook assumption.\nNo regional rollout or retailer acceptance promise. Scope must be written before activation.\nNetherfield + Rowantree\nPENDING SCOPE\nSlotting support coordinates requirements and documents opportunities.\nProposed service process.\nMust state payment does not buy, secure, or guarantee placement; retailer retains decision. Written brand approval before spend/commitment.\nTanneryside / Netherfield\nCLEAR WITH CONTROL\nCategory data informs assortment, pricing, velocity, replenishment, retention review.\nProposed decision-support use; data availability is entry condition.\nData, forecasts, and scenarios are not guarantees of sales or distribution. No comparative or outcome claim without documented basis.\nRowantree + Tanneryside\nCLEAR WITH CONTROL\nField team checks authorized execution, records evidence, reports exceptions, recommends correction.\nProposed operating activity; retailer/site permission may apply.\nRecommendations stay nonbinding until accepted. Do not claim display or shelf result without evidence and authorization.\nRowantree\nCLEAR WITH CONTROL\nRetention = activated doors still carrying approved SKU set / activated doors; closures/delistings count as not retained.\nProspective pilot KPI definition.\nReport retailer disposition; do not represent forecast retention as achieved result.\nRowantree\nCLEAR\nBase economics: $17,452 gross sales; $1,080 trade reserve; $4,020 Rowantree charges; $12,352 net proceeds.\nWorkbook Base assumptions: 54 doors, 6 weeks, 9 units/week, $6.50, 92% retention, 90% feasibility.\nIllustrative/founder-editable only. No actual rate, spend, sales, or commitment claim. Maintain formula and approval record.\nNetherfield\nPENDING FOUNDER INPUT\nContinue / adjust / stop gates: retention and feasibility thresholds.\nProspective governance design; workbook formulas.\nNot a commercial guarantee. Stop for unresolved material readiness or authorization issue.\nNetherfield + Rowantree\nCLEAR\nCalifornia compliance wording and records process.\nOperational interpretation as of 15 Feb 2025.\nDo not say compliance guarantees retailer acceptance, legality of a specific promotion, or results. Tanneryside to resolve open questions.\nTanneryside\nPENDING CLEARANCE\nDeliberate non-promises: no retailer placement, acceptance, footprint, personnel, launch recovery, customer result, sales outcome, or distribution outcome is represented as committed. Rowantree may recommend timely actions; Netherfield approval is mandatory before financial or external commitments.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/netherfield_pilot_economics.xlsx","bytes":9358,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/ad6c37ba7b5ab8681f993e74d337e49b9f3e152d3c33e85125ab2aa8e0f7ecce.xlsx","sha256":"ad6c37ba7b5ab8681f993e74d337e49b9f3e152d3c33e85125ab2aa8e0f7ecce","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Pilot model","row_count":32,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Netherfield Industries | California-first pilot economics","","","",""]},{"r":"2","cells":["Editable planning model | 6-week pilot | All numeric values are illustrative assumptions / founder-supplied inputs, not historical facts or commitments.","","","",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["Initial scope excludes Nevada and Arizona because Rowantree coverage is thin. Inclusion requires documented verification and separate written approval.","","","",""]},{"r":"5","cells":["Input / output","Downside","Base","Upside","Notes"]},{"r":"6","cells":["ASSUMPTIONS - edit blue cells","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Pilot duration (weeks)","6","6","6","Bounded period"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Activated California doors","36","54","72","Named doors only; illustrative"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Units / door / week","6","9","12","Illustrative velocity"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Net sales / unit","6.5","6.5","6.5","Founder-supplied price assumption"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Distribution retention at review","0.68","0.92","0.96","Activated doors still carrying approved SKU set"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Coverage feasibility factor","0.55","0.9","0.98","Execution feasibility; Nevada/AZ not in scope"]},{"r":"13","cells":["Retailer trade / slotting reserve","900","1080","1440","Third-party promotional spend; written brand approval required"]},{"r":"14","cells":["Rowantree setup charge","1500","1500","1500","Rowantree service charge"]},{"r":"15","cells":["Rowantree service fee / activated door","30","30","30","Rowantree service charge"]},{"r":"16","cells":["Field execution cost","1200","900","750","Rowantree execution charge"]},{"r":"17","cells":["DECISION THRESHOLDS","","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Continue retention threshold","0.85","0.85","0.85","At or above"]},{"r":"19","cells":["Adjust retention threshold","0.7","0.7","0.7","70%-84%; below = stop"]},{"r":"20","cells":["Continue coverage feasibility threshold","0.8","0.8","0.8","At or above"]},{"r":"21","cells":["Adjust coverage feasibility threshold","0.6","0.6","0.6","60%-79%; below = stop"]},{"r":"22","cells":["CALCULATED OUTPUTS - formulas","","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["Gross sales","=B8*B7*B9*B10*B11  [缓存: 5728.32]","=C8*C7*C9*C10*C11  [缓存: 17437.68]","=D8*D7*D9*D10*D11  [缓存: 32348.16]","Doors x weeks x units x price x retention; feasibility controls decision gate"]},{"r":"24","cells":["Retailer trade / slotting spend","=B13  [缓存: 900]","=C13  [缓存: 1080]","=D13  [缓存: 1440]","Separate from Rowantree charges"]},{"r":"25","cells":["Rowantree service fee","=B8*B15  [缓存: 1080]","=C8*C15  [缓存: 1620]","=D8*D15  [缓存: 2160]","Activated doors x service fee / door"]},{"r":"26","cells":["Rowantree charges total","=B14+B25+B16  [缓存: 3780]","=C14+C25+C16  [缓存: 4020]","=D14+D25+D16  [缓存: 4410]","Setup + service fee + field execution"]},{"r":"27","cells":["Net brand proceeds","=B23-B24-B26  [缓存: 1048.32]","=C23-C24-C26  [缓存: 12337.68]","=D23-D24-D26  [缓存: 26498.16]","Gross sales less trade spend and Rowantree charges"]},{"r":"28","cells":["Retention decision","=IF(B11>=B18,\"Continue\",IF(B11>=B19,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Stop]","=IF(C11>=C18,\"Continue\",IF(C11>=C19,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Continue]","=IF(D11>=D18,\"Continue\",IF(D11>=D19,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Continue]","Formula-driven gate"]},{"r":"29","cells":["Coverage decision","=IF(B12>=B20,\"Continue\",IF(B12>=B21,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Stop]","=IF(C12>=C20,\"Continue\",IF(C12>=C21,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Continue]","=IF(D12>=D20,\"Continue\",IF(D12>=D21,\"Adjust\",\"Stop\"))  [缓存: Continue]","Formula-driven gate"]},{"r":"30","cells":["Overall gate","=IF(OR(B28=\"Stop\",B29=\"Stop\"),\"STOP\",IF(AND(B28=\"Continue\",B29=\"Continue\"),\"CONTINUE\",\"ADJUST\"))  [缓存: STOP]","=IF(OR(C28=\"Stop\",C29=\"Stop\"),\"STOP\",IF(AND(C28=\"Continue\",C29=\"Continue\"),\"CONTINUE\",\"ADJUST\"))  [缓存: CONTINUE]","=IF(OR(D28=\"Stop\",D29=\"Stop\"),\"STOP\",IF(AND(D28=\"Continue\",D29=\"Continue\"),\"CONTINUE\",\"ADJUST\"))  [缓存: CONTINUE]","Continue / Adjust / Stop"]},{"r":"31","cells":["Approval boundary","Written brand approval required before any trade spend, slotting, retailer-facing or external commitment.","","","Rowantree may recommend actions; recommendations are not commitments."]},{"r":"32","cells":["Model note","No retailer acceptance, placement, sales, or distribution is guaranteed. Category data and scenario outputs are decision support only.","","","California controls: see pitch and approval register."]},{"r":"33","cells":["","","","",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/rowantree_services_pitch.pdf","bytes":15582,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/8d723b4f17ba554708f6c39646afb9b40507ecf0ac74faaae1c842c090fb9227.pdf","sha256":"8d723b4f17ba554708f6c39646afb9b40507ecf0ac74faaae1c842c090fb9227","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"ROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE\nRowantree Grocery Cooperative | proposed service provider\n\n\n\n\nA controlled market-entry pilot\nfor Netherfield Industries\n\nA six-week, California-first services pilot designed to test execution quality\nand distribution retention before any wider commitment.\n\n\n\n\n     The candid starting point\n     Our coverage is thin in Nevada and Arizona. Our last two brand launches lost distribution within a year. This\n     proposal does not explain away either fact or promise an outcome.\n\n\n\n\nPrepared for Juno Blackwood, Founder | Discussion draft for Tanneryside Advisory clearance by 21 March 2025, 5:00 p.m.\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nThe decision is a test, not a leap\n\nFounder outcome: decide whether Rowantree can earn a broader role through observable, governed execution.\n\n\n\n\n  Authorize now                               Learn during pilot                          Decide at gates\n  Authorize a defined six-week                Test approved scope, readiness, field       Continue, adjust, or stop using\n  California-first pilot planning phase. No   verification, early velocity signals, and   pre-agreed thresholds. Nevada and\n  retailer, slotting, or trade-spend          the percentage of activated doors           Arizona remain excluded unless\n  commitment is authorized by this            retained at each review point.              coverage is separately verified and\n  decision.                                                                               approved in writing.\n\n\n\n\n  What Rowantree is proposing\n  Not freight with nicer slides: a launch operating loop that coordinates retailer requirements and authorized slotting\n  opportunities, uses category evidence to recommend decisions, verifies in-store work, and sends exceptions to\n  the people who can act.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                     Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 2 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nThe risks are visible before approval\n\n\n\n   Coverage limitation: Nevada and Arizona\n   Rowantree’s coverage is thin in Nevada and Arizona. We have not assumed a footprint, personnel, facility, or retailer\n   access there. Those states are outside the initial pilot; any later inclusion requires documented coverage verification and a\n   separate written authorization.\n\n\n\n\n   Launch-history disclosure\n   Rowantree’s last two brand launches lost distribution within a year. We do not have a validated causal analysis or a\n   documented recovery result to offer. The response here is prospective: narrow the scope, make readiness and execution\n   evidence visible, inspect leading indicators weekly, and let the founder stop or adjust before a regional rollout.\n\n   Retention definition\n   At each review, retained distribution = activated pilot doors still carrying the approved SKU set / activated pilot doors. Confirmed\n   closures, delistings, or non-carrying doors count as not retained; retailer disposition is recorded, not assumed.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                      Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 3 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nOne operating loop around a launch\n\n\n\n  1 | Opportunity and authorization                         2 | Decision support                       3 | Field proof and correction\n  Rowantree coordinates retailer                            Category data informs assortment,          Field activity checks authorized\n  requirements and assesses an                              introductory pricing, velocity review,     shelf/display execution, captures photo or\n  opportunity. It documents terms and                       replenishment questions, and retention     issue evidence where permitted, reports\n  presents any slotting or trade request to                 risk. Data, forecasts, and modeled         exceptions, and recommends corrective\n  Netherfield for written approval before                   scenarios are not guarantees of sales or   actions. Recommendations are proposals\n  any commitment.                                           distribution.                              until accepted.\n\n\n\n\n   Important boundary\n   Slotting support or payment does not buy, secure, or guarantee shelf placement. Retailers retain their own requirements\n   and decisions. Rowantree does not speak for a retailer, waive its requirements, or assure acceptance of Netherfield\n   products.\n\n   Category data is not a guarantee of sales or distribution.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                   Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 4 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nBounded pilot: California-first, six weeks\n\nScope is a planning assumption to be confirmed in writing: one approved SKU set, named California doors only, six weeks\n\n\n                                Agreed named-door scope; inventory/readiness confirmation; approved external claims; available\n      Before activation\n                                category/scan data; written budget and approval protocol; retailer terms documented.\n\n                                Map requirements, confirm no-cost versus paid actions, capture baseline activated doors, release only\n      Weeks 1-2 | setup\n                                approved materials and spend.\n\n                                Field checks and exception log; weekly velocity, availability, execution, and retention review;\nWeeks 3-5 | execute & measure\n                                Rowantree recommends timely remedies for Netherfield decision.\n\n                                Joint review against thresholds; continue to a separately authorized next phase, adjust within scope, or\n        Week 6 | gate\n                                stop. No automatic extension.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 5 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nControl stays with the brand\n\n\n\n   Operating ownership\n\n   Netherfield              Provides inventory/readiness, approved claims and data; approves trade spend, slotting, retailer-facing\n                            commitments, and material corrective actions in writing.\n\n   Rowantree                Coordinates requirements, proposes category and merchandising actions, executes only authorized activity,\n                            maintains evidence and exception log, measures and reports.\n\n   Joint founders / leads   Weekly working review; decision gates and exceptions. Tanneryside Advisory reviews unresolved legal or\n                            promotional questions.\n\n\n\n\n   Escalation and cadence\n   Rowantree reports a material KPI miss, retailer issue, execution failure, or unapproved-spend request within one business\n   day to Netherfield’s pilot lead. No external or financial commitment proceeds without written brand approval. Weekly\n   working reviews examine the log; a week-3 checkpoint can pause or adjust execution.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                 Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 6 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nEconomics are an editable decision tool\n\n\n   Base scenario: illustrative, six-week, California-first\n   The linked workbook uses founder-editable assumptions, not actual Netherfield results, Rowantree fees, retailer terms, or\n   commitments. Headline values below reconcile to the Base column of the workbook.\n\n\n\n\n  Gross sales                         54 activated doors x 6 weeks x 9 units/door/week x $6.50 x 92% retention = $17,438\n\n\n  Trade / slotting reserve            $1,080 | separately approved retailer or promotional spend; no placement is promised\n\n\n  Rowantree charges                   $4,020 | $1,500 setup + $1,620 service fee + $900 field execution\n\n\n  Net brand proceeds                  $12,338 | gross sales less listed trade spend and Rowantree charges\n\n\n   Decision thresholds used in the workbook\n   Continue only if retention is at least 85%, coverage feasibility is at least 80%, and no material unapproved commitment exists. Adjust if\n   retention is 70%-84% or feasibility is 60%-79%. Stop below either lower bound or when a material readiness/authorization issue remains\n   unresolved.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                     Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 7 of 8\n\fROWANTREE GROCERY COOPERATIVE | PROPOSED SERVICES PILOT\n\n\n\n\nThe founder decision requested\n\n\n\n   Authorize a controlled planning pilot\n   Authorize Rowantree and Netherfield to finalize the named California-door scope, readiness checklist, and Base\n   scenario assumptions for a six-week pilot. This authorization is not approval of retailer terms, slotting, trade spend, or\n   any external commitment. Each requires Netherfield’s written approval first.\n\n\n\n\n   Claim and promotion discipline\n   California trade-promotion and advertising treatment as of 15 February 2025: external promotional, comparative, performance, or\n   outcome claims require a reasonable documented basis, approved wording, and retained approval records before use. This sales\n   proposal is not legal advice. Tanneryside Advisory clears unresolved legal or promotional questions; compliance does not\n   guarantee retailer acceptance or commercial results.\n\n\n\n\n                     Meeting output: a bounded written authorization, or a clear decision not to proceed.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                              Founder meeting | 25 March 2025 | 8 of 8\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All three required files exist at the top level with the exact requested filenames and are valid, readable files of their stated formats.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Working-directory file listing and successful opening or parsing of each file.","grader_hint":"Confirm exact case-sensitive filenames, parse the PDF, open the workbook, and inspect the DOCX package."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The founder-facing PDF contains no more than eight pages, counting the cover and any appendix.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PDF page count.","grader_hint":"Use PDF introspection rather than counting visual section headings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The claims and commitments register contains no more than two rendered pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX to PDF or inspect it in a word processor with normal pagination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch is written specifically for a skeptical founder deciding whether to engage Rowantree, rather than as an internal strategy deck or a generic distributor capabilities presentation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pitch framing, language, proof posture, and decision content.","grader_hint":"Look for founder-level concerns such as control, risk, accountability, retained distribution, and what is actually being authorized."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pitch clearly identifies Netherfield Industries as the prospective brand and Rowantree Grocery Cooperative as the proposed service provider.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Named parties in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Accept possessive or abbreviated references after the full names first appear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch states a concrete founder-relevant outcome for the proposed engagement, not merely a list of Rowantree capabilities.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening proposition and pilot outcome language.","grader_hint":"A credible outcome can concern disciplined market entry, measurable distribution retention, controlled trade spend, or another decision-relevant result; it must not be an unsupported guarantee."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package distinguishes the full-stack offer from freight hauling by explaining how slotting support, category data, and in-store merchandising work together around a brand launch.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service description in the pitch.","grader_hint":"Credit an integrated operating proposition, not three disconnected service labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Slotting support is described in operationally meaningful terms such as opportunity assessment, retailer requirement coordination, authorization, documentation, or performance review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pitch service description.","grader_hint":"The material should clarify what Rowantree would actually do without implying that payment secures placement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Category-data support is tied to legitimate decisions such as assortment, velocity, pricing, replenishment, or distribution retention rather than presented as decorative analytics.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pitch service description and metrics.","grader_hint":"At least one concrete decision use must be apparent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"In-store merchandising support defines observable field activity and verification, rather than promising only unspecified execution.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pitch service description.","grader_hint":"Examples include authorized display execution, shelf checks, photo evidence, corrective follow-up, or issue reporting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pitch expressly acknowledges that Rowantree’s coverage is thin in Nevada and Arizona.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Explicit state-specific coverage statement in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Both states must be named; a generic reference to coverage gaps is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Nevada and Arizona coverage gap is presented early enough and prominently enough that it is not buried as fine print.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Location and visual treatment of the coverage disclosure.","grader_hint":"Credit if a founder reviewing the core proposition would encounter the limitation before being asked to approve the pilot."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package offers a credible way to contain or manage the thin-coverage risk without claiming unverified personnel, facilities, retailer access, or geographic reach.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Coverage mitigation and pilot design.","grader_hint":"Accept a narrowed footprint, staged activation, explicit service-level limitations, partner verification, or another defensible mitigation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pitch expressly acknowledges that Rowantree’s last two brand launches lost distribution within a year.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Historical disclosure in the PDF.","grader_hint":"The meaning must be direct; euphemisms such as 'mixed launch history' do not earn full credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch does not invent causes, recovery results, or corrective outcomes for the two failed launches and clearly distinguishes known history from interpretation or proposed controls.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Failure-history discussion and related qualifications.","grader_hint":"Credit transparent uncertainty and prospective controls; do not require a specific disclaimer phrase."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The response to the prior launch failures includes concrete retention controls that would reveal underperformance early enough to act.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pilot governance, metrics, and review cadence.","grader_hint":"Look for leading indicators, accountable review, intervention triggers, or staged continuation rather than a vague promise to monitor results."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch defines distribution retention in measurable terms suitable for a pilot review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"KPI definitions in the pitch.","grader_hint":"A usable definition should identify the unit being retained, the measurement point or interval, and how closures or delistings are treated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed pilot is bounded by scope rather than amounting to an open-ended regional rollout.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pilot proposition in the PDF and model.","grader_hint":"Scope can be bounded by geography, accounts, doors, products, duration, spend, or a defensible combination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pilot scope reflects the disclosed coverage limitations rather than quietly assuming uniform execution across all target states.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Relationship between coverage disclosure and pilot scope.","grader_hint":"The package should either limit initial scope or visibly account for differentiated execution capacity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch provides a workable sequence from authorization through setup, field execution, measurement, and review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pilot timing or operating sequence.","grader_hint":"Exact dates are not required, but the sequence must support execution without leaving major phases undefined."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package identifies material pilot entry conditions that must be resolved before commitments or spend are activated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pilot prerequisites in the pitch or register.","grader_hint":"Examples include agreed scope, approved budget, retailer terms, data availability, inventory readiness, or approved claims."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package includes continuation, adjustment, or stop criteria tied to observed pilot performance or execution feasibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision gates in the pitch and model.","grader_hint":"Credit explicit decision logic; a general promise to review the pilot is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The founder is asked to make a specific, bounded decision in the meeting.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call to action in the pitch.","grader_hint":"The ask should state what is being authorized or agreed and should not require approval of unknown or unlimited commitments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pitch makes clear that Netherfield must approve trade-spend or slotting expenditures before Rowantree commits the brand.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Approval boundary in the pitch.","grader_hint":"Look for a mandatory written or otherwise auditable brand authorization boundary, not merely consultation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package distinguishes mandatory brand approval from Rowantree’s ability to recommend merchandising or account actions without portraying every recommendation as a binding commitment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Language governing approvals and recommendations.","grader_hint":"The must/should boundary should be operationally clear: financial or external commitments require approval, while evidence-led recommendations remain proposals until accepted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pitch actively states that slotting support or payment does not buy, secure, or guarantee shelf placement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Explicit warning in the PDF.","grader_hint":"The statement must discourage the misuse, not merely describe slotting activity neutrally."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pitch actively states that category data, forecasts, or modeled scenarios are not guarantees of sales or distribution.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Explicit data-use qualification in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that directly rejects using analytics as a guaranteed outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package avoids implying that Rowantree can speak for retailers, waive retailer requirements, or assure acceptance of Netherfield products.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Retailer-facing claim posture across the pitch and register.","grader_hint":"Award credit when retailer decisions are consistently described as outside Rowantree’s unilateral control."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Promotional, comparative, performance, and outcome claims are framed as requiring a reasonable documented basis before external use.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compliance language and claims register.","grader_hint":"Look for substantiation discipline consistent with California advertising requirements, not merely a generic 'subject to legal review' footer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The compliance treatment identifies California and the stated as-of date of 15 February 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction and date in the pitch or claims register.","grader_hint":"Both the jurisdiction and date must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package treats California advertising and trade-promotion compliance as a constraint on claim wording, approvals, and recordkeeping rather than claiming that compliance itself guarantees commercial acceptance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compliance application across deliverables.","grader_hint":"Credit practical application to the proposal; unsupported legal conclusions do not satisfy the item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any legal characterization is appropriately limited and routes unresolved legal or promotional questions to Tanneryside Advisory rather than presenting the sales package as legal advice.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pitch qualifications and approval register.","grader_hint":"Tanneryside should have a meaningful approval or escalation role, not just a name in a footer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package assigns practical responsibilities between Netherfield and Rowantree for data, inventory or readiness, approvals, execution, measurement, and review.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roles or operating model in the pitch.","grader_hint":"A full RACI matrix is not required, but each major activity must have a discernible owner."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The operating model provides an escalation path for execution failures, unapproved spend, retailer issues, or material KPI misses.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Governance language in the pitch.","grader_hint":"Look for who is notified, what kind of issue triggers escalation, and how action is authorized."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package establishes a review cadence appropriate to detecting launch and retention problems before the end of the pilot.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Meeting or reporting cadence.","grader_hint":"The cadence must be more specific than 'regular updates' and proportionate to the proposed pilot duration."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains editable input cells and functioning formulas rather than a static table or image of projected economics.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas, cell types, and protection state.","grader_hint":"Inspect formulas and change at least one material input to confirm dependent outputs recalculate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook includes the material commercial drivers needed to evaluate the pilot, including scale or doors, sales or velocity, trade spend, Rowantree charges, and field-execution cost or an explained equivalent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook input and calculation structure.","grader_hint":"The model need not use these exact labels, but it must expose the main revenue, spend, fee, and execution drivers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook presents at least three distinguishable scenarios, including a downside case, and each scenario’s outputs derive from its corresponding assumptions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario inputs, formulas, and outputs.","grader_hint":"Trace scenario references or change inputs to verify that outputs are not manually copied."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Projected gross sales or equivalent top-line value equals the model’s applicable scale multiplied through the stated sales or velocity assumptions over the modeled period, within ±1% allowing for clearly disclosed rounding or ramp factors.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas and assumption labels.","grader_hint":"Use the model’s own units and period; accept an equivalent auditable formulation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Net brand proceeds or equivalent economic output reconciles from gross value less the modeled trade spend, service fees, and other explicitly identified deductions, within ±1%.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formulas and summary outputs.","grader_hint":"Recalculate using displayed inputs and deductions; do not impose an unstated accounting definition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook clearly distinguishes Rowantree service charges from retailer trade spend or slotting amounts.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook labels and calculations.","grader_hint":"The founder should be able to see which amounts compensate Rowantree and which are promotional expenditures or third-party costs."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Every material numerical input not provided in the request is visibly labeled as an assumption, illustrative value, or founder-supplied input rather than as an actual Netherfield or Rowantree result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook labels, notes, and pitch footnotes.","grader_hint":"Review especially doors, velocity, prices, fees, trade spend, conversion, and retention rates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The model allows the founder to see how weaker coverage or lower retention changes the economics or continuation decision.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario or sensitivity treatment in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Credit an explicit sensitivity, downside scenario, or decision threshold connected to these risks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any headline economics shown in the pitch match the corresponding workbook scenario and period within ±1%.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Values and labels in the PDF compared with workbook outputs.","grader_hint":"Compare like-for-like scenario, scope, and period; if the pitch intentionally contains no headline economics, this item is not earned."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The claims register identifies each material external claim or commitment in the pitch and gives enough wording or context to recognize it.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Claims register entries compared with the PDF.","grader_hint":"Sample the coverage, launch-history, service, economics, slotting, data, and pilot claims; the register need not repeat purely decorative copy."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"For each material claim, the register records its basis or assumption and any qualification needed for external use.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim basis and qualification fields or equivalent structure.","grader_hint":"A blanket statement that all claims are illustrative is insufficient where claims have different bases or limitations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The register records an approval owner and a usable status for claims or commitments that require review before the meeting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ownership and status information in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Statuses may use any clear vocabulary, but the reviewer must be able to distinguish cleared material from open or withheld material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The register documents deliberate wording changes, qualifications, or withheld promises made to avoid overstating coverage, launch performance, retailer authority, slotting outcomes, category-data predictions, or commercial figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change, qualification, or non-promise records.","grader_hint":"Look for substantive claim-control decisions, not cosmetic editing notes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Coverage limitations, pilot scope, approval boundaries, commercial assumptions, and decision gates are mutually consistent across the pitch, workbook, and claims register.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-file comparison of core terms and claims.","grader_hint":"Check that no file silently expands geography, changes the approval rule, presents an assumption as actual, or uses a different pilot period or scenario without explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package is concise, candid, visually legible, and usable by Ingrid Wainwright in one founder meeting without requiring her to improvise material qualifications.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall rendered package and the completeness of its decision narrative.","grader_hint":"Assess whether a skeptical founder could understand the offer, limitations, economics, controls, and requested decision without asking the author to reconcile contradictions."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Rowantree Grocery Cooperative is seeking its first regional-brand client for an expanded service offering beyond freight. The package must win founder confidence while remaining commercially and legally defensible under external compliance review.","difficulty_sources":["Building founder credibility while disclosing two commercially damaging weaknesses","Separating mandatory approval rights from nonbinding sales and merchandising recommendations","Actively correcting common misuse of slotting support and category analytics","Creating decision-useful economics without representing invented figures as facts","Maintaining consistent scope, claims, assumptions, and commitments across three files","Applying California claim-substantiation and trade-promotion discipline without legal overclaiming"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"A wholesale-trade sales manager packages a founder-facing proposal, editable pilot model, and internal claims approval record without supplied company data.","intended_verdict":"A strong package earns credibility by disclosing Rowantree’s two material weaknesses before asking for a bounded pilot, then contains those risks through measurable governance rather than unsupported reassurance.","required_tensions":["The package must sell expanded services while candidly naming thin Nevada and Arizona coverage.","The package must acknowledge that the last two launches lost distribution within a year without inventing causes, lessons already proven, or recovery outcomes.","Paid slotting support and category analytics must be actively prevented from being used as promises of shelf placement, sales, or distribution.","Netherfield approval is mandatory before trade-spend or external commitments are made, while Rowantree may recommend timely merchandising actions that remain nonbinding until accepted."],"gold_relationships":["Any pitch economics must agree with the corresponding workbook scenario, scope, and period within the stated tolerance.","Gross modeled value must derive from the workbook’s stated scale and sales or velocity assumptions, with any ramp factors visible.","Net proceeds or equivalent output must reconcile from gross value less identified trade spend, service fees, and other deductions.","A downside scenario must degrade at least one risk-relevant driver and flow through formulas to its outputs.","Pilot continuation, adjustment, or stop logic must connect to measurable outputs or operational feasibility.","Every material external claim or commitment in the pitch must be traceable to a basis, qualification, owner, and review status in the claims register.","The geography, duration, commercial scenario, authorization boundary, and decision gates must agree across all three deliverables."],"professional_content_expected":["An integrated description of slotting support, category-data use, and field merchandising that goes beyond freight.","A bounded pilot with prerequisites, ownership, operating sequence, review cadence, leading indicators, and decision gates.","A measurable treatment of distribution retention and a mechanism for detecting launch underperformance early.","A clear distinction between retailer decisions, brand approvals, Rowantree recommendations, and Rowantree execution responsibilities.","California-oriented claim substantiation, approval, and recordkeeping discipline as of 15 February 2025 without overreaching into unsupported legal conclusions.","An editable scenario model that distinguishes assumptions from facts and separates Rowantree fees from retailer or trade-promotion spending.","A claim-control record documenting substantive qualifications and promises deliberately withheld from the external deck."],"imperfections_to_preserve":["No actual footprint figures, retailer commitments, customer results, commercial rates, or Netherfield operating data are available.","The two weak-coverage states are known, but the magnitude of the gaps is not.","The failure outcome of the two prior launches is known, but causes and corrective results are not.","The package must therefore use clearly labeled illustrative assumptions rather than fabricating evidence."],"space_feasibility":"The eight-page pitch can accommodate the proposition, integrated services, candid risk disclosures, bounded pilot, governance, economics summary, and founder decision at normal presentation density. The two-page register can use a compact table covering material claims rather than every sentence.","offline_validation":"An imagined reference solution can be created and rendered offline using Python spreadsheet and document libraries plus a local office renderer. Formulas, page limits, scenario relationships, cross-file values, and text disclosures can all be inspected without network access."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"founder_pitch","filename":"rowantree_services_pitch.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"Founder-facing services pitch deck for Netherfield Industries.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum eight pages, including any cover or appendix. It must be usable in the founder meeting without relying on unsupported verbal qualifications."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"pilot_economics","filename":"netherfield_pilot_economics.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"Editable scenario model for evaluating a bounded full-stack services pilot.","required":true,"constraints":["Inputs, assumptions, formulas, scenarios, and decision outputs must be distinguishable. Unknown commercial figures must not be represented as historical or committed facts."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"claims_register","filename":"claims_and_commitments_register.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Internal approval record for the claims, qualifications, commitments, assumptions, and deliberate non-promises in the package.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum two pages and suitable for review by Tanneryside Advisory before the founder meeting."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"sales_proposal","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"sales_managers","sector":"wholesale_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":8.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"A wholesale sales leader should review commercial credibility and founder usability; a sales-operations or trade-promotion compliance reviewer should separately review claim discipline, authorization boundaries, California applicability, and cross-file consistency.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No source files or company operating data are supplied, so the quality of numerical values cannot be judged as historical truth. Review instead whether unknowns are transparently modeled as editable assumptions, whether formulas reconcile, and whether external claims remain supportable and appropriately qualified."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:20:39+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:20:39+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:20:39+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:20:39+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R14']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:20:39+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/3627188f405b6042","declared_deliverables":["rowantree_services_pitch.pdf","netherfield_pilot_economics.xlsx","claims_and_commitments_register.docx"]};
